      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you are describing as seeing heat signatures or hearing electrical melodies are actually known aspareidolia and synesthesia, where the brain mistakenly interprets random sensory data. While real thermal imaging requires specialized equipment, your brain often fills in dark gaps with imagined patterns or sounds based on past experiences and expectations. Although it would be unusual to feel this everything this vividly without a device nearby, it doesn't necessarily mean something supernatural is happening; however, if these sensations become persistent, overwhelming, or affect your daily life, it is highly recommended to consult a medical professional to rule out underlying neurological conditions.",
